  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Most emeralds have a garden inside.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "gem",
        "shape": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "garden": true,
        "color": "#c8dc3c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Gem dealers call it the jardin, French for garden.",
      "say": "Gem dealers call it the zhar-dan, French for garden.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Jardin",
        "sub": "French for garden",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It's the pattern of inclusions and fractures inside the stone.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "halo": "#d7ffe3",
        "garden": true,
        "label": "Inside the stone",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "GIA says emeralds usually show inclusions to the unaided eye.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "lab",
        "name": "GIA gem lab",
        "role": "Emerald, under a loupe",
        "color": "#5bb4e8",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#eef2f4",
            "hair": "updo",
            "hairColor": "#2e2420",
            "skin": "#c98e6a",
            "expression": "focused",
            "glasses": "loupe",
            "prop": "gem",
            "propTone": "#1f9d62"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "An eye-clean emerald is rare, so it's especially valuable.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "ring",
        "shape": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Eye-clean",
        "velvet": "#ec6a9c",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Most are treated by filling the cracks with oil or resin.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cut",
        "phase": "blade",
        "place": "Filled with oil",
        "pieces": [
          {
            "tone": "#1f9d62"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#a98be0"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The emerald cut was developed for emeralds,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "gift",
        "stone": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "to": "The emerald cut",
        "date": "For emeralds",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "with its corners cut off to prevent chipping.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "ring",
        "shape": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "metal": "white",
        "label": "Corners cut off",
        "velvet": "#5bb4e8",
        "color": "#f0552e"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Some Colombian emeralds hold a gas bubble and a salt crystal.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "gem",
        "shape": "emerald",
        "tone": "#1f9d62",
        "light": "#d7ffe3",
        "garden": true,
        "label": "Bubble and crystal",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Labs use that garden to tell natural emeralds from lab-grown ones.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "lab",
        "name": "A fingerprint",
        "role": "The garden inside",
        "color": "#c8dc3c",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#eef2f4",
            "hair": "short",
            "hairColor": "#2e2420",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "proud",
            "glasses": "loupe",
            "prop": "magnifier"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "caption": "Almost every emerald has a garden inside: the jardin, a web of inclusions and fractures. It decides how the stone is treated, how it's cut and how labs tell it's natural.",
